 "readme": "![LES2 Banner](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/les2feup/guidelines/main/src/figures/les2banner.png)\n\n# Generative AI for Climate-Resilient Urban Emergency Planning\n\n[![Python 3.12](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.12-blue.svg)](https://www.python.org/downloads/release/python-3120/)\n[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](LICENSE)\n[![Git LFS](https://img.shields.io/badge/dataset-Git%20LFS-8A2BE2.svg)](https://git-lfs.com)\n\nGenerative AI evaluation framework for emergency response scenarios across five municipalities in metropolitan Porto, Portugal. Trains and compares five tabular generative model families — GaussianCopula, CTGAN, TVAE, ForestDiffusion, and TabSyn — on a published real-world emergency events dataset, assessed across fidelity, utility, privacy, and energy cost dimensions.\n\n## Installation\n\nRequires [Git LFS](https://git-lfs.com) to fetch the published dataset.\n\n```bash\ngit clone git@github.com:joaocarlos/genai-urban-emergency-planning.git\ncd genai-urban-emergency-planning\ngit lfs pull\npython -m venv .venv\nsource .venv/bin/activate\npip install -e .\n```\n\nCTGAN and TVAE require a separate environment due to a `synthcity` dependency conflict:\n\n```bash\npython -m venv .venv_synthcity\nsource .venv_synthcity/bin/activate\npip install synthcity\n```\n\n## Reproducing Results\n\nRun notebooks sequentially from the project root:\n\n```bash\nsource .venv/bin/activate\n\n# Stages 1–4: data ingestion → published dataset\njupyter nbconvert --to notebook --execute notebooks/01_source_standardization.ipynb\njupyter nbconvert --to notebook --execute notebooks/02_spatial_grid.ipynb\njupyter nbconvert --to notebook --execute notebooks/03_dataset_enrichment.ipynb\njupyter nbconvert --to notebook --execute notebooks/04_dataset_preparation.ipynb\n\n# Stage 5: generative model training\njupyter nbconvert --to notebook --execute notebooks/05a_gaussiancopula.ipynb\n.venv_synthcity/bin/python -m jupyter nbconvert --to notebook --execute notebooks/05b_ctgan.ipynb\n.venv_synthcity/bin/python -m jupyter nbconvert --to notebook --execute notebooks/05c_tvae.ipynb\npython scripts/patch_synthcity_tvcomplement.py   # fix TVComplement scores post-hoc\njupyter nbconvert --to notebook --execute notebooks/05d_forestdiffusion.ipynb\njupyter nbconvert --to notebook --execute notebooks/05e_tabsyn.ipynb\n\n# Stage 6–8: evaluation, demonstrations, scenario map\njupyter nbconvert --to notebook --execute notebooks/06_model_evaluation.ipynb\njupyter nbconvert --to notebook --execute notebooks/07_demonstrations.ipynb\njupyter nbconvert --to notebook --execute notebooks/08_scenario_map.ipynb\n```\n\n## Usage\n\nThe published dataset is available in `data/published/` and can be loaded directly:\n\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\nevents = pd.read_parquet(\"data/published/events.parquet\")\ntrain  = pd.read_parquet(\"data/published/splits/events_random_split.parquet\")\n```\n\nSee [`data/published/DATASET_CARD.md`](data/published/DATASET_CARD.md) for full schema and provenance details.\n\n## Contribution\n\nThis repository accompanies a scientific publication. Bug reports and questions are welcome via [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/joaocarlos/genai-urban-emergency-planning/issues).\n\n## License\n\nThis project is licensed under the MIT License — see the [LICENSE](LICENSE) file for details.\n",
